' =====================================================================
' RoboFetch - Sequence diagram: C3, physical delivery verification
'
' Deliberately simplified to the CONCEPT rather than every retry and
' edge case: two independent pieces of real-world evidence - the
' gripper joint's own reported state, and the parcel's real position
' in the simulator - are checked before an order is ever marked
' complete. Neither is the command pipeline that asked for the work.
' (Does not show: the up-to-3-attempts release retry loop, or the
' "joint never reported at all" fallback - see gripper_node.py's
' on_release() and task_manager.py's execute_order() for those.)
'
' Arrowheads carry real meaning here, same convention as
' 03-sequence-order-success.puml: a filled head (->) is a synchronous
' call the sender waits on; an open head (->>) is a one-way ROS topic
' publish that gets no reply at all. Gazebo NEVER answers a question -
' it only ever broadcasts state on its own topics, independent of
' whether anyone is listening at that moment. The gripper and task
' manager only ever PUBLISH into that space and separately, passively,
' read whatever the last broadcast happened to say - which is exactly
' why a settle-time wait and a distance check are needed at all,
' instead of a single trustworthy reply.
' =====================================================================
@startuml
skinparam backgroundColor White
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam sequence {
  ArrowColor #34495E
  LifeLineBorderColor #7F8C8D
  ParticipantBorderColor #34495E
  ParticipantBackgroundColor #FBFCFE
}

participant "Task Manager\n(the brain)" as TM
participant "Gripper Node\n(the hand)" as GR
participant "Gazebo\n(the real world)" as GZ

TM -> GR ++ : release(parcel)  -- a real\nservice call, TM waits
GR ->> GZ : publish "detach"\n(fire and forget, no reply)
GR -> GR : wait the settle time
GZ -->> GR : the joint broadcasts its OWN\nstate on a separate topic:\n"detached"
GR --> TM -- : released, and I confirmed it\nagainst the joint's own state

note over GR, GZ
  EVIDENCE #1: the gripper's own joint broadcast
  "detached" on its own - not a reply to the
  detach command, and not just "I sent it".
end note

TM -> TM : wait 1 s for the physics to settle
GZ -->> TM : the parcel's pose, broadcast\non its own topic all along\n(Task Manager just reads\nthe latest value)

TM -> TM : measure distance from that position\nto the delivery bay

note over TM, GZ
  EVIDENCE #2: the parcel's REAL position,
  overheard from Gazebo's own broadcast - never
  requested, and never "I drove to the right spot".
end note

alt close enough to the bay
  TM -> TM : mark the order COMPLETED
else too far away
  TM -> TM : mark the order FAILED\n(it was never actually carried)
end

@enduml
